# Refactoring Base PHP API

This plan outlines the steps to modernize the PHP API base, focusing on security, modularity, and maintainability.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Breaking Changes**: The directory structure for `routes` and `services` will change. [sqlProcedures.php](file:///d:/xampp/base-apis/sqlProcedures.php) will be deleted.
> **Configuration**: Secrets (DB credentials, Tokens) will be moved to a configuration file that should **NOT** be committed to version control.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Cleanup and Security
#### [DELETE] [sqlProcedures.php](file:///d:/xampp/base-apis/sqlProcedures.php)
- This file contains insecure SQL string concatenation and is actively unused (commented out in code).
- **Action**: Delete the file.

#### [MODIFY] [const.php](file:///d:/xampp/base-apis/const.php)
- Enhance to look for a local configuration file (e.g., `config.local.php`) for secrets.
- If the local file exists, load constants from there.
- Add `config.local.php` to [.gitignore](file:///d:/xampp/base-apis/.gitignore).

### 2. Modular Architecture
#### [NEW] [Router.php](file:///d:/xampp/base-apis/routes/Router.php)
- Create a `Router` class to handle URI parsing and dynamic dispatching.
- Replace the giant `switch` statement in [routes.php](file:///d:/xampp/base-apis/routes/routes.php).

#### [MODIFY] [routes/routes.php](file:///d:/xampp/base-apis/routes/routes.php)
- Update to use the new `Router` class.
- Register routes dynamically (e.g., `$router->get('/users', 'UserController::getAll')`).

#### [Refactor Services]
- Move logic from [services/get.php](file:///d:/xampp/base-apis/routes/services/get.php), [post.php](file:///d:/xampp/base-apis/routes/services/post.php) into dedicated Controllers inside `routes/controllers/`.
- Example: `routes/controllers/UserController.php`.

## Verification Plan
### Manual Verification
- **Test Endpoints**: Use Postman or CURL to verify that existing endpoints (`/users`, `/login`, etc.) still work after refactoring.
- **Security Check**: Verify that sensitive tokens are not exposed in the source code.
